mudlark NEWS

Version 0.4.0 (unreleased)
--------------------------
* Inline mode. mudlark now paints into the terminal's primary screen buffer
  instead of the alternate screen: server output and local echo go to the
  terminal's own scrollback, and the live frame is just the divider and the
  input line at the bottom. Selection, scrollback, search and scrolling are
  the terminal's own — the in-app viewport, its copy mode and its mouse
  reporting are gone, and what mudlark prints survives `:quit`.
* Drag-selection with the left button no longer belongs to mudlark: use the
  terminal's own selection (hold Shift where the terminal sends the mouse to
  applications).
* Escape sequences in server output are now filtered by boba rather than
  being written through untouched: SGR styling is kept, while cursor
  movement, erase-in-line, OSC (window titles, hyperlinks), DCS and APC are
  dropped, as are stray control bytes below 0x20. A lone CR still ends a row.
  This is a deliberate limitation: an already-rendered MUD prompt keeps its
  colors but cannot repaint the screen around itself.
* Server line endings are normalized before they reach the scrollback.
  Carrion Fields ends its rows with LF CR, and CR LF and LF CR are now the
  same single row break whichever order the server used; a CR NUL pair (NVT's
  bare CR) loses its NUL, and repeated terminators still mean blank lines.
  Before, an LF CR pair produced a blank row between every line.
* `termcap` API break for user scripts. Removed: `'type`, `'encoding`,
  `'color-level`, `'256color?`, `'unicode?`, `'describe`. Added:
  `'width-model` (the cell-width model boba pinned: `"grid"`, `"wcwidth"` or
  `"uts51"`). `'truecolor?` now answers from boba's terminal capability
  profile. `'fg-color` and `'bg-color` take an optional fourth argument: the
  ANSI16 slot used when the terminal is not truecolor.
* Colors have two tiers. A color is an `(R G B SLOT)` list: the exact RGB
  triple on a truecolor terminal, the slot below it. There is no 256-color
  tier and no RGB-to-palette matching any more, so a 256-color terminal that
  does not advertise truecolor gets the 16 slots. The `*color-*` defvars in
  `lisp/init.lisp` carry slots; a three-element list still works and simply
  has no color below truecolor.
* The startup banner reports the cell-width model and `truecolor` or
  `16-color` instead of `$TERM`, the color level and the encoding.
* mudlark no longer detects terminal capabilities itself: width model,
  truecolor and size all come from boba, which probes once at startup.
* The Kitty keyboard protocol, bracketed paste, Ctrl+D (delete-char) and
  Ctrl+C (discard the line) behave exactly as before.
* boba floor is 0.9.0, ditty floor is 0.7.3.

Version 0.1.0 (unreleased)
--------------------------
* Initial release
* Core RFC 854 telnet client functionality
* TUI interface with boba textinput input
* Lisp scripting via ditty integration
* TinTin++ compatible MUD scripting support
